<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
	targetNamespace="http://www.blogger.com/atom/ns#"
	xmlns:blogger="http://www.blogger.com/atom/ns#"
	xmlns:draft="http://purl.org/atom-blog/ns#"
	xmlns:jxb="http://java.sun.com/xml/ns/jaxb"
	jxb:version="1.0"
	elementFormDefault="unqualified">
	<xs:import namespace="http://purl.org/atom-blog/ns#" schemaLocation="bloggerDraft.xsd"/>
	<xs:element name="bloggerExtension">
		<xs:complexType>
			<xs:sequence>
				<xs:element ref="blogger:convertLineBreaks" >
					<xs:annotation>
						<xs:documentation><![CDATA[ 
This flag, when set to true, means that a blog's posts will have their newlines automatically converted to
 <br />. If set to false, newlines will not be transformed. 
 This flag is read-only and can only be changed through the Blogger web interface for now. 
 You can see a blog's Line Break status by sending a GET to it's service.feed URI and looking 
 for it as a child of the &lt;feed> element:
<br/>
    &lt;convertLineBreaks xmlns="http://www.blogger.com/atom/ns#">true&lt;/convertLineBreaks>

						]]> 
						</xs:documentation>
					</xs:annotation>				
				</xs:element>
				<xs:element ref="draft:draft" >
					<xs:annotation>
						<xs:documentation><![CDATA[ 
Blogger Draft extension. <br/> http://purl.org/atom-blog/ns#
<br/> Set to true to indicate a draft, false otherwise.
						]]> 
						</xs:documentation>
					</xs:annotation>				
				</xs:element>
			</xs:sequence>
		</xs:complexType>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:annotation>
		<xs:documentation>
			Blogger Atom extension http://code.blogger.com/archives/atom-docs.html#extensions
		</xs:documentation>
	</xs:annotation>
 	<xs:element name="convertLineBreaks" type="xs:boolean" />
</xs:schema>
